# SECRETS-001 (S-12): a pattern with no leading "**/" only matches at the context root, unlike
# .gitignore's equivalent syntax — confirmed empirically with `docker build` against a scratch
# context containing a nested `sub/.env.local` and `sub/foo.pem`, both of which leaked into the
# build context under the previous root-only patterns. Every pattern below is anchored with
# "**/" so it matches at any depth, and both the root and nested forms are listed explicitly so
# this stays correct even if Docker's globbing semantics change.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/*.crt
**/.aws
**/.ssh
**/.env.local.seed-client-secret
